en:
And then I was back in the reflection room.
"Are you all right, {a}?"
Iwashita glanced at my face.{p}

"Is something wrong with her hand?
She isn't holding anything, is she?"
Arai muttered under his breath.{p}

When I stepped into the hallway, Hashimoto was nowhere to be seen.
Where did she go?
Maybe I should try going back to the classroom.{p}

"Ah, wait a second!"
As I reached out to catch her, the textbook fell from my hand.
When she saw it, her face went rigid.{p}

"That's..."
She pointed at the textbook on the floor.
Can she tell it's Kawahara's textbook?{p}

"It's not that I want to curse anyone.
I did something terrible to Kawahara.
I'm not allowed to go on living."{p}

...As she said it, a teacher I'd never seen before appeared behind her.
"Hashimoto, what are you doing?
You were supposed to report to the reflection room today."{p}

"Hashimoto!"
I tried to tear up the apology letter lying in front of her.
The moment I did, I was engulfed in a blinding light.{p}

No, I can't get near her☆
What's happening?
My head hurts☆{p}

.........When the light died down and I opened my eyes, Fukuzawa was peering down at me.
"Thank goodness, {b}.
I thought you were never going to wake up."{p}

It was too dark to see clearly, but inside the shoe locker was a pair of eyes, completely dried out.
Not just eyes.
Clean-cut eyebrows, a shapely nose, purple lips...{p}

Shindo was there, strung up from it.
Blood was streaming from his ears and eyes.
He looked like the picture on a tarot card.{p}

His thin back.
If I shoved him away and ran, could I get out of this strange place?
...I'm not so sure I could.{p}

I slowly opened the stall door.
...No one's there.
So Hosoda hasn't been killed?{p}

You actually believe Arai's story?
Well, whatever. Either way, you're going to be killed.
Why, you ask?{p}

Still, where should I go now?
As I walked down the hallway for a while, I suddenly heard Kawahara's voice.
"I see. So that's what you think..."{p}

What had Kawahara wanted me to help him with?
Hashimoto had been so terribly depressed. Maybe he wanted me to be there for her...
People called him two-faced, but maybe deep down he was a good person after all.{p}

When I looked at Hashimoto's apology letter, there was a single photograph tucked inside.
Kawahara and Hashimoto were standing side by side in the darkness.
Did Hashimoto end up killing herself after all?{p}In the photo, the two of them were smiling sadly.{p}

No, I can't get near her☆
What's happening?
My head hurts☆{p}
